return A.c(A.nQ(m,"how_to_play",'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang="en">\n<head>\n  <meta charset="UTF-8">\n  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">\n  <title>T-G-Apps Canasta How to Play</title>\n  <style>\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 16px;\n      background: #f6f1e4;\n      color: #111827;\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      line-height: 1.45;\n    }\n\n    .tgapps-policy-page {\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 900px;\n      margin: 0 auto;\n    }\n\n    .hero,\n    .card {\n      display: block;\n      width: auto;\n      margin: 0 0 14px 0;\n      padding: 14px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n      background: #ffffff;\n      border: 1px solid #D4AF37;\n    }\n\n    .hero {\n      background: #063a25;\n      color: #ffffff;\n    }\n\n    .badge {\n      display: none;\n    }\n\n    h1, h2, h3 {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n      color: #063a25;\n    }\n\n    .hero h1,\n    .hero h2 {\n      color: #ffd966;\n    }\n\n    p {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n    }\n\n    ul {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 22px;\n      padding: 0;\n    }\n\n    li {\n      margin-bottom: 5px;\n    }\n\n    a {\n      color: #0b63ce;\n      word-break: break-word;\n    }\n\n    .footer {\n      text-align: center;\n      color: #ffffff;\n      background: #063a25;\n      padding: 12px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class="tgapps-policy-page">\n    <section class="hero">\n      <h1>T-G-Apps LLC</h1>\n      <h2>T-G-Apps Canasta How to Play</h2>\n      <p class="subtitle">Meld cards of a rank with your partner, build canastas of seven, and go out first.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>1. Goal</h3>\n      <p>Four players play in two partnerships: Player 1 (South) and Player 3 (North) against Player 2 (West) and Player 4 (East). Partners meld together and score together. When a side reaches 5000 points (or 2500 in a shorter game) at the end of a hand, the side with more points wins.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>2. Setup Options</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Players: </strong>each of the four players has a name and a type. Player 1 is always a person; tap the Type button to switch any other player between Human and Robot. If more than one person plays, pass the phone when the game asks you to.</li>\n        <li><strong>Points to win: </strong>5000, or 2500 for a shorter game.</li>\n        <li><strong>Music: </strong>Background music on or off, and its volume.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>3. The Cards</h3>\n      <p>Canasta uses two decks and four jokers: 108 cards. Each player gets 11. Jokers and 2s are wild. Card values: joker 50; aces and 2s 20; kings down to 8s 10; 7s down to 4s and black 3s 5.</p>\n      <p><strong>Red 3s</strong> are laid down as soon as you get them, and you draw a card to replace each one. They are worth 100 each (800 for all four), but count against a side that has not melded by the end of the hand.</p>\n      <p><strong>Black 3s</strong> stop the next player from taking the pile. They can only be melded when going out.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>4. Your Turn</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Draw: </strong>take the top card of the stock, or take the whole discard pile (see below).</li>\n        <li><strong>Meld: </strong>lay down 3 or more cards of the same rank, or add cards to your side\'s melds. A meld needs at least 2 natural cards and may hold no more than 3 wild cards. Each side has one meld of each rank.</li>\n        <li><strong>Discard: </strong>end your turn by putting one card on the pile.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>Tap cards to pick them, then press Meld or Discard.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>5. Opening</h3>\n      <p>A side\'s first melds each hand must be worth at least a minimum that depends on its score: 15 below 0, 50 up to 1495, 90 from 1500 and 120 from 3000. You can put down several melds to reach it. If they fall short, press Take Back before you discard.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>6. Taking the Pile</h3>\n      <p>Pick the cards from your hand that go with the top card of the pile, then press Take the Pile. The top card is melded with them and the rest of the pile goes to your hand. You can never take the pile when its top card is a black 3 or a wild card.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Frozen pile: </strong>before your side has opened, or while a wild card or red 3 is in the pile, you need a natural pair matching the top card. To open with the pile, the top card, your pair and any other melds from your hand must reach your minimum.</li>\n        <li><strong>Otherwise: </strong>you can take it with a natural pair, a natural card and a wild card, or when the top card fits one of your side\'s melds.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>7. Canastas and Going Out</h3>\n      <p>A meld of 7 or more cards is a canasta: 500 points if natural, 300 if mixed. Your side needs a canasta to go out; you may complete it on that turn. Go out by melding everything, or keeping one final discard. With an empty stock, you must take a legal unfrozen pile whose top fits your existing meld; otherwise you may end the hand. Drawing the last stock card as a red 3 ends the hand immediately.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>8. Scoring</h3>\n      <p>Add melded card values, canasta bonuses, red 3s and 100 for going out; subtract both partners\u2019 remaining cards. Concealed going out earns 200: you must not have melded on an earlier turn or added to your partner\u2019s earlier melds, and must complete your own canasta on the finishing turn. After a stock draw, this concealed finish may bypass the opening minimum.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>9. Hints and Robots</h3>\n      <p>Hints and robots use the same engine to compare legal plays, including pile pickups, melds, wild-card use and discards. They use only the acting player\u2019s hand and public information, including remembered cards from earlier pile pickups. Hidden hands and future stock cards are sampled as possibilities, never read from the actual game.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>10. Games History</h3>\n      <p>Every finished game is saved with each side\'s final score. Games History lists the newest games first.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- tgapps-room-how-to-play 11 -->\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>Responsible Play</h3>\n      <p>T-G-Apps Canasta is an entertainment game. It does not offer real-money gambling, prizes, wagers or cash-out functionality.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <p class="footer">\xa9 2026 T-G-Apps LLC. All rights reserved.</p>\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>\n',"tgapps_canasta_engine"),$async$Lu)
