return A.c(A.nQ(m,"how_to_play",'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang="en">\n<head>\n  <meta charset="UTF-8">\n  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">\n  <title>T-G-Apps Indian Rummy How to Play</title>\n  <style>\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 16px;\n      background: #f6f1e4;\n      color: #111827;\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      line-height: 1.45;\n    }\n\n    .tgapps-policy-page {\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 900px;\n      margin: 0 auto;\n    }\n\n    .hero,\n    .card {\n      display: block;\n      width: auto;\n      margin: 0 0 14px 0;\n      padding: 14px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n      background: #ffffff;\n      border: 1px solid #D4AF37;\n    }\n\n    .hero {\n      background: #063a25;\n      color: #ffffff;\n    }\n\n    .badge {\n      display: none;\n    }\n\n    h1, h2, h3 {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n      color: #063a25;\n    }\n\n    .hero h1,\n    .hero h2 {\n      color: #ffd966;\n    }\n\n    p {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n    }\n\n    ul {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 22px;\n      padding: 0;\n    }\n\n    li {\n      margin-bottom: 5px;\n    }\n\n    a {\n      color: #0b63ce;\n      word-break: break-word;\n    }\n\n    .footer {\n      text-align: center;\n      color: #ffffff;\n      background: #063a25;\n      padding: 12px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class="tgapps-policy-page">\n    <section class="hero">\n      <h1>T-G-Apps LLC</h1>\n      <h2>T-G-Apps Indian Rummy How to Play</h2>\n      <p class="subtitle">Arrange all 13 cards into sequences and sets, with a pure sequence, and declare before anyone else.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>1. Goal</h3>\n      <p>Indian Rummy is played with 13 cards. Be the first to arrange your whole hand into sequences and sets and declare. This is pool rummy: the other players score points for the cards they could not meld, and a player who reaches the limit (101 or 201) is out. The last player left wins.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>2. Setup Options</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Number of players: </strong>2 to 6.</li>\n        <li><strong>Players: </strong>each player has a name and a type. Player 1 is always a person; tap the Type button to switch any other player between Human and Robot. If more than one person plays, pass the phone when the game asks you to.</li>\n        <li><strong>Out at: </strong>101, or 201 for a longer game.</li>\n        <li><strong>Music: </strong>Background music on or off, and its volume.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>3. Cards and Wild Cards</h3>\n      <p>The game uses two decks and two printed jokers. After the deal, one card is cut and shown face up: every card of its rank is wild for the hand, and so are the printed jokers. If the cut card is a joker, aces are wild. Wild cards are marked W in your hand.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Pure sequence: </strong>3 or more cards of one suit in a row with no wild card standing in, such as 4-5-6 of hearts. Aces are low (A-2-3) or high (Q-K-A).</li>\n        <li><strong>Sequence: </strong>the same, with wild cards filling gaps.</li>\n        <li><strong>Set: </strong>3 or 4 cards of one rank in different suits, wild cards allowed.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>4. Your Turn</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Draw: </strong>take the top card of the stock, or the top discard. A wild card on the discard pile cannot be taken.</li>\n        <li><strong>Discard or declare: </strong>tap a card and press Discard. If all your other 13 cards are in sequences and sets, with at least two sequences and one of them pure, press Declare instead.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>Your hand is arranged for you: pure sequences outlined in light blue, other sequences in purple, sets in green, then the cards that do not fit.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>5. Scoring</h3>\n      <p>The player who declares scores nothing. Every other player with two sequences, one of them pure, scores only the cards they could not meld; without them, every card counts. Aces and face cards count 10, other cards their number, wild cards nothing, and no one scores more than 80 in a hand. Low scores are good.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>6. Hints and Robots</h3>\n      <p>Press Hint for advice on your draw and your discard. The recommended button or card is outlined in white. Robots use the same reasoning, and the Hint shows it with the numbers. They count the unseen cards, wild cards included, that could still complete each sequence or set, keep wild cards and the cards of a pure sequence, take a discard only when it beats an average card from the stock, avoid throwing a card the next player can use, and declare as soon as they can.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>7. Games History</h3>\n      <p>Every finished game is saved with each player\'s final score. Games History lists the newest games first.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- tgapps-room-how-to-play 8 -->\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>Responsible Play</h3>\n      <p>T-G-Apps Indian Rummy is an entertainment game. It does not offer real-money gambling, prizes, wagers or cash-out functionality.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <p class="footer">\xa9 2026 T-G-Apps LLC. All rights reserved.</p>\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>\n',"tgapps_indian_rummy_engine"),$async$LP)
