return A.c(A.nQ(m,"how_to_play",'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang="en">\n<head>\n  <meta charset="UTF-8">\n  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">\n  <title>T-G-Apps Pinochle How to Play</title>\n  <style>\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 16px;\n      background: #f6f1e4;\n      color: #111827;\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      line-height: 1.45;\n    }\n\n    .tgapps-policy-page {\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 900px;\n      margin: 0 auto;\n    }\n\n    .hero,\n    .card {\n      display: block;\n      width: auto;\n      margin: 0 0 14px 0;\n      padding: 14px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n      background: #ffffff;\n      border: 1px solid #D4AF37;\n    }\n\n    .hero {\n      background: #063a25;\n      color: #ffffff;\n    }\n\n    .badge {\n      display: none;\n    }\n\n    h1, h2, h3 {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n      color: #063a25;\n    }\n\n    .hero h1,\n    .hero h2 {\n      color: #ffd966;\n    }\n\n    p {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n    }\n\n    ul {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 22px;\n      padding: 0;\n    }\n\n    li {\n      margin-bottom: 5px;\n    }\n\n    a {\n      color: #0b63ce;\n      word-break: break-word;\n    }\n\n    .footer {\n      text-align: center;\n      color: #ffffff;\n      background: #063a25;\n      padding: 12px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class="tgapps-policy-page">\n    <section class="hero">\n      <h1>T-G-Apps LLC</h1>\n      <h2>T-G-Apps Pinochle How to Play</h2>\n      <p class="subtitle">Bid, name trump, show your meld, and take the aces, tens and kings in tricks with your partner.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>1. Goal</h3>\n      <p>Four players play in two partnerships: Player 1 (South) and Player 3 (North) against Player 2 (West) and Player 4 (East). Your side scores points for meld and for the counters it takes in tricks. The first side to reach 1500 points (or 1000 in a shorter game) wins. If both sides get there on the same hand, the side that won the bid wins.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>2. Setup Options</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Players: </strong>each of the four players has a name and a type. Player 1 is always a person; tap the Type button to switch any other player between Human and Robot. If more than one person plays, pass the phone when the game asks you to.</li>\n        <li><strong>Points to win: </strong>1500, or 1000 for a shorter game.</li>\n        <li><strong>Music: </strong>Background music on or off, and its volume.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>3. The Deck and the Deal</h3>\n      <p>Pinochle uses 48 cards: two each of the 9, jack, queen, king, 10 and ace in every suit. Each player gets 12 cards. From high to low the cards rank A, 10, K, Q, J, 9. The deal passes to the left each hand.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>4. Bidding and Trump</h3>\n      <p>Starting left of the dealer, each player bids or passes. The first bid is at least 250 and each bid is at least 10 higher. Once you pass you are out of the bidding. When only one bidder is left, they win the bid and name the trump suit. If everyone passes, the dealer must take the bid at 250.</p>\n      <p>Set the amount with the \u2212 and + buttons, then press Bid, or press Pass.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>5. Meld</h3>\n      <p>After trump is named, every player shows their meld. A card can count once in each of the three groups below.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Trump: </strong>run (A, 10, K, Q, J of trump) 150, double run 1500; royal marriage (K and Q of trump) 40; marriage (K and Q of another suit) 20; dix (9 of trump) 10 each.</li>\n        <li><strong>Around: </strong>one of a rank in every suit. Aces 100, kings 80, queens 60, jacks 40. Double (two of each) aces 1000, kings 800, queens 600, jacks 400.</li>\n        <li><strong>Pinochle: </strong>the queen of spades with the jack of diamonds, 40; double pinochle 300.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>A side\'s meld only counts if it takes at least one trick.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>6. The Play</h3>\n      <p>The winning bidder leads the first trick. The winner of each trick leads the next.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li>You must follow suit. If you can beat the card that is winning the trick, you must.</li>\n        <li>If you have none of the suit led, you must play a trump, beating any trump already played if you can.</li>\n        <li>If you have neither, play any card.</li>\n        <li>The highest trump wins; otherwise the highest card of the suit led. Of two identical cards, the first one played wins.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>Your playable cards lift up; tap one to play it.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>7. Scoring</h3>\n      <p>Aces, tens and kings are counters, worth 10 each to the side that takes them, and the last trick is worth 10: 250 in all. Each side adds its meld (if it took a trick) and its counters.</p>\n      <p>The side that won the bid must reach its bid with meld and counters. If it does, it scores its total; if not, it goes set and loses the amount of its bid. The other side always scores what it made.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>8. Hints and Robots</h3>\n      <p>Press Hint for advice on your bid, your trump suit or your card. The recommended button or card is outlined in white. Robots use the same reasoning, and the Hint shows it with the numbers. They deal the unseen cards many times, in ways that fit the meld shown and the suits each player could not follow, and play the hand out with each choice. They bid only as high as they make most of the time, name the trump suit that makes the bid most often, and play the card that scores best.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>9. Games History</h3>\n      <p>Every finished game is saved with each side\'s final score. Games History lists the newest games first.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- tgapps-room-how-to-play 10 -->\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>Responsible Play</h3>\n      <p>T-G-Apps Pinochle is an entertainment game. It does not offer real-money gambling, prizes, wagers or cash-out functionality.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <p class="footer">\xa9 2026 T-G-Apps LLC. All rights reserved.</p>\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>\n',"tgapps_pinochle_engine"),$async$Lz)
