s=3
return A.c(A.nQ(m,"how_to_play",'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang="en">\n<head>\n  <meta charset="UTF-8">\n  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">\n  <title>T-G-Apps Rummy 500 How to Play</title>\n  <style>\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 16px;\n      background: #f6f1e4;\n      color: #111827;\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      line-height: 1.45;\n    }\n\n    .tgapps-policy-page {\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 900px;\n      margin: 0 auto;\n    }\n\n    .hero,\n    .card {\n      display: block;\n      width: auto;\n      margin: 0 0 14px 0;\n      padding: 14px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n      background: #ffffff;\n      border: 1px solid #D4AF37;\n    }\n\n    .hero {\n      background: #063a25;\n      color: #ffffff;\n    }\n\n    .badge {\n      display: none;\n    }\n\n    h1, h2, h3 {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n      color: #063a25;\n    }\n\n    .hero h1,\n    .hero h2 {\n      color: #ffd966;\n    }\n\n    p {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n    }\n\n    ul {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 22px;\n      padding: 0;\n    }\n\n    li {\n      margin-bottom: 5px;\n    }\n\n    a {\n      color: #0b63ce;\n      word-break: break-word;\n    }\n\n    .footer {\n      text-align: center;\n      color: #ffffff;\n      background: #063a25;\n      padding: 12px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class="tgapps-policy-page">\n    <section class="hero">\n      <h1>T-G-Apps LLC</h1>\n      <h2>T-G-Apps Rummy 500 How to Play</h2>\n      <p class="subtitle">Meld as much as you can: every card you put down scores for you.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>1. Goal</h3>\n      <p>Score points by melding sets (3 or 4 of a rank) and runs (3 or more of a suit in a row) and by laying cards off on any meld. When a hand ends, each player scores the cards they melded and laid off, less the cards left in their hand. The first player to 500 points wins.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>2. Setup Options</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Number of players: </strong>2 to 6.</li>\n        <li><strong>Players: </strong>each player has a name and a type. Player 1 is always a person; tap the Type button to switch any other player between Human and Robot. If more than one person plays, pass the phone when the game asks you to.</li>\n        <li><strong>Points to win: </strong>500, or 250 for a shorter game.</li>\n        <li><strong>Music: </strong>Background music on or off, and its volume.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>3. The Deal and the Discard Pile</h3>\n      <p>Each player gets 13 cards with two players and 7 with more. One card starts the discard pile. The discard pile is spread out so every card in it can be seen.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>4. Your Turn</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Draw: </strong>take the top card of the stock, or tap any card in the discard pile to take it and every card above it. If you take more than the top card, you must meld or lay off the deepest card you took before you discard.</li>\n        <li><strong>Meld and lay off: </strong>put down sets and runs, and add cards to any meld on the table. Aces are low (A-2-3) or high (Q-K-A), but a run cannot go round the corner (K-A-2).</li>\n        <li><strong>Discard: </strong>end your turn with one card on the discard pile. You cannot throw back the single card you just took.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>5. Scoring</h3>\n      <p>The hand ends when a player has no cards left, or when the stock runs out. Card values: aces 15 (1 when melded in A-2-3), face cards 10, other cards their number. Every card you melded or laid off counts for you; every card left in your hand counts against you. Your score can go below zero.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>6. Hints and Robots</h3>\n      <p>Press Hint for advice on your draw, your melds or your discard. The recommended button or cards are outlined in white. Robots use the same reasoning, and the Hint shows it with the numbers. They take from the discard pile when the melds are worth more than the cards they must carry, meld whatever they can, count the unseen cards that could still complete each meld, and avoid throwing a card the next player can use, judging from the cards that player took and passed on.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>7. Games History</h3>\n      <p>Every finished game is saved with each player\'s final score. Games History lists the newest games first.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- tgapps-room-how-to-play 8 -->\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>Responsible Play</h3>\n      <p>T-G-Apps Rummy 500 is an entertainment game. It does not offer real-money gambling, prizes, wagers or cash-out functionality.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <p class="footer">\xa9 2026 T-G-Apps LLC. All rights reserved.</p>\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>\n',"tgapps_rummy_500_engine"),$async$LZ)
