return A.c(A.nQ(m,"how_to_play",'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang="en">\n<head>\n  <meta charset="UTF-8">\n  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">\n  <title>T-G-Apps Rummy How to Play</title>\n  <style>\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 16px;\n      background: #f6f1e4;\n      color: #111827;\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      line-height: 1.45;\n    }\n\n    .tgapps-policy-page {\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 900px;\n      margin: 0 auto;\n    }\n\n    .hero,\n    .card {\n      display: block;\n      width: auto;\n      margin: 0 0 14px 0;\n      padding: 14px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n      background: #ffffff;\n      border: 1px solid #D4AF37;\n    }\n\n    .hero {\n      background: #063a25;\n      color: #ffffff;\n    }\n\n    .badge {\n      display: none;\n    }\n\n    h1, h2, h3 {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n      color: #063a25;\n    }\n\n    .hero h1,\n    .hero h2 {\n      color: #ffd966;\n    }\n\n    p {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n    }\n\n    ul {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 22px;\n      padding: 0;\n    }\n\n    li {\n      margin-bottom: 5px;\n    }\n\n    a {\n      color: #0b63ce;\n      word-break: break-word;\n    }\n\n    .footer {\n      text-align: center;\n      color: #ffffff;\n      background: #063a25;\n      padding: 12px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class="tgapps-policy-page">\n    <section class="hero">\n      <h1>T-G-Apps LLC</h1>\n      <h2>T-G-Apps Rummy How to Play</h2>\n      <p class="subtitle">Make sets and runs, and be the first to get rid of your cards.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>1. Goal</h3>\n      <p>Be the first player to put down all of your cards. The player who goes out scores the points left in everyone else\'s hand. The first player to reach the target score wins the game.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>2. Setup Options</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Number of players: </strong>2 to 6.</li>\n        <li><strong>Players: </strong>each player has a name and a type. Player 1 is always a person; tap the Type button to switch any other player between Human and Robot. If more than one person plays, pass the phone when the game asks you to.</li>\n        <li><strong>Points to win: </strong>50, 100 or 200.</li>\n        <li><strong>Robot skill: </strong>Beginner, Intermediate or Expert. All robots play at the same level.</li>\n        <li><strong>Show hints: </strong>on or off. Turn hints off to test your own skill.</li>\n        <li><strong>Discard History: </strong>on or off (off at first). When it is on, a Discard History button shows every card discarded this hand, who discarded it, and who took it.</li>\n        <li><strong>Music: </strong>Background music on or off, and its volume.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>3. The Deal</h3>\n      <p>Each player gets 10 cards with two players, 7 with three or four, and 6 with five or six. One card is turned face up to start the discard pile; the rest are the stock. The player to the dealer\'s left goes first, and the deal passes to the left each hand.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>4. Your Turn</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Draw: </strong>take the top card of the stock, or the top card of the discard pile.</li>\n        <li><strong>Meld: </strong>put down a set (3 or 4 cards of the same rank) or a run (3 or more cards of one suit in a row). Aces are low: A-2-3 is a run, Q-K-A is not.</li>\n        <li><strong>Lay off: </strong>add a card to any meld on the table, yours or anyone else\'s. If the card fits two melds, the game asks which one.</li>\n        <li><strong>Discard: </strong>end your turn by putting one card on the discard pile. You cannot throw back the card you just took from the discard pile.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p><strong>Melding is your choice. </strong>You do not have to put down a meld as soon as you have one. You may keep it in your hand and put it down on a later turn. This has a risk: if another player goes out first, that player also scores the points of the cards you kept. Putting a meld down early has a cost too: other players can then lay off cards on it.</p>\n      <p>Tap cards in your hand to pick them, then press Meld, Lay Off or Discard.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>5. Going Out and Scoring</h3>\n      <p>You go out when your last card is melded, laid off or discarded. You then score the points left in every other hand: face cards 10, aces 1, and other cards their number.</p>\n      <p>If the stock runs out, the discard pile (except its top card) is shuffled into a new stock. This can happen up to six times in a hand; after that, the hand ends and nobody scores.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>6. Hints and Robots</h3>\n      <p>Press Hint for advice on your turn: the whole turn, and the reasons for it. The recommended button or cards are outlined. Hints always give the advice of the Expert robot.</p>\n      <p>Beginner robots take a discard only when it completes a meld or fits a meld on the table, put down melds as soon as they can, and discard high cards. Intermediate and Expert robots remember every discard. They may keep a meld in their hand, and they avoid discarding cards that help the next player. Expert robots also think through many possible ways the hand could go.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>7. Games History</h3>\n      <p>Every finished game is saved with each player\'s final score. Games History lists the newest games first.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- tgapps-room-how-to-play 8 -->\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>Responsible Play</h3>\n      <p>T-G-Apps Rummy is an entertainment game. It does not offer real-money gambling, prizes, wagers or cash-out functionality.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <p class="footer">\xa9 2026 T-G-Apps LLC. All rights reserved.</p>\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>\n',"tgapps_rummy_engine"),$async$M8)
